'The new canonical detecting representation is the action on N^ab of rank97, for N=ker q12. Modulus576 is sufficient on H; the explicit sufficient full-group modulus is 2^51942*3^14136. The proof uses integral graph homology, H1(Q,M)=0, H2(Q,M)=Z/96, a frame-separating quotient, and genuine tangential specialization. The raw rational homology has no Delta constituent, despite this action-level detection.','',
'The uniform integral Burau theorem strengthens the separate two-adic and odd-field tests: LI.9 gives one actual Delta1 witness at EVERY prime and every congruence level for the primitive-cube-root family. The proof uses an integral triangular flag, square-zero unipotents, the ramified3 residue, and R2 with compatible normal cores. The latest timed assessment records the next concrete mixed-primary route.','',
'The exact Ferrari kernel is C=C2*C2*C2, with C-prime=K-prime K-squared free of rank5. Its geometric cover is [2]:E minus E[2] to E minus O. Every odd relative pro-prime completion over a purely forgetful base kills C. Retaining C-ab first produces an actual order1944 mixed quotient, but its pentagon is exactly the previous order216 affine equation. The complete class-two characteristic3 stage is also insufficient. These are exact marked quotient comparisons, not dimension heuristics.','',
'The stronger all-prime result constructs one actual k_rel with Delta1 and pentagon product1 in L/R_nil(C-prime), and proves directly that its braid formulas define an automorphism of this quotient fixing C/R_nil(C-prime) pointwise. It can simultaneously retain the entire adelic Burau conclusion. The proof uses the exact braid centre, pro-prime automorphism kernels, a signed idempotent seed, R2, compactness, and centrelessness. Any next finite target must retain a nonnilpotent image of C-prime.','',
'The next completed target takes D=C-double-prime(C-prime)-squared, of rank129, and its characteristic3 homology. Literal L-relators are checked. In the harmonic pair, w=[[x,y],x[x,y]x-inverse] has order12; a=w^6 and its xy-inverse conjugate are involutions whose product has order6. Thus the pair second-derived subgroup is not nilpotent. An independent implementation confirms the certificate. The effect lies in boundary/proper coupling on two16-dimensional character blocks and vanishes after compactification. A canonical compact2-dimensional quotient proves that no source word with q12 value5I can lie in the full harmonic evaluation kernel. This blocks that seed method only. Subsequent exact normalization proves that the24 two-branch blocks factor through L/C-prime and their pentagon is automatic; the nonnilpotent pair property alone does not add a parity relation. The whole linear action kills the resulting pentagon defect because it lies in D. The actual affine quotient C/(D-prime D-cubed) retains the D-translation discarded by linear homology. Its escape is now proved by a cyclic controlled seed whose normal image is nilpotent in all30 pair/core tests. Exact transfer and congruence kernels upgrade this to one actual Delta1 witness on the whole L/D-prime quotient, with an actual automorphism fixing C/D-prime. The next specified cover is D4=C-double-prime(C-prime)-fourth-powers, tested through full Fox chains rather than homology alone.','',
'The fourth-power cover D4=C-double-prime(C-prime)-fourth-powers has index8192 in C and rank4097. All1024 character blocks retain five Fox chain coordinates over F9. The joint target, including the earlier affine rank5 factor, has kernel on C exactly D4-prime D4-cubed. A complete conditional proof transfers triviality of the two braid conjugators to an actual automorphism of L/(D4-prime D4-cubed). The harmonic pure character permutation groups have order32 and class2; they are not abelian. The old cyclic seed S fails here: u=S-cubed and v=(X2 X1)u(X2 X1)-inverse are involutions whose product has order9 on a literal five-chain block and its four-dimensional cycle subspace, and order3 on its proper three-dimensional quotient. Two independent exact implementations verify the counterexample. This excludes that seed from every normal nilpotent pair subgroup; it does not exclude another seed, assert that the retained actual gentle witness fails this pentagon, or decide Delta on GT.','',
'The obstruction is removed by a new actual seed, not by altering the five pentagon values independently. The B-normal closure of S has primitive proper images supported on40 harmonic orbits, all explicitly conjugate to one centreless simple group of order6048. Its full primitive chain image under all30 marked source maps is a finite3-extension of a perfect simple-factor product, so it has noC2 quotient. Goursat therefore supplies an element of this genuine source normal closure with signed value5I and trivial entire primitive chain image modulo3. It preserves every earlier normal source condition. Exact Gaussian-integer Fox identities and the normal pro3 congruence kernel extend the argument to every prime power. R2 and compactness then give one actual Delta1 gentle witness satisfying the pentagon in L/D4-prime, retaining Zhat^4097, and defining an actual automorphism fixing C/D4-prime. This closes the entire fourth-power relative abelian family. The next test reverses the prime order, using D3=C-double-prime(C-prime)-cubed and characteristic2 full chains; its outcome is not yet assigned.','',
